      "text": "To find \\( f(3) \\), we start by using the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\nFirst, we substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\quad \\text{(1)} \\]\nNext, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\quad \\text{(2)} \\]\nWe now have a system of two equations:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27, \\]\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\]\nWe can solve this system by eliminating \\( f(-2) \\). Multiply the second equation by 2:\n\\[ 2f(-2) + 4f(3) = 24. \\quad \\text{(3)} \\]\nNow subtract equation (1) from equation (3):\n\\[ (2f(-2) + 4f(3)) - (f(3) + 2f(-2)) = 24 - 27, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ 3f(3) = -3, \\]\nso:\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{-1}. \\]",
